"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan with an initial budget of $500,000 for phase one, kicking off on June 15th. The project team was expanded by five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with an onboarding session scheduled for September 10th. Significant progress was reported in phase two regarding predictive analytics, with a detailed presentation planned for November 20th. The project recently completed its testing phase, celebrated on October 10th, and is now moving into the development phase under the guidance of lead developer Omar Jensen. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November. Additionally, security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year, and a training budget of $15,000 has been approved for the coding team and project managers, starting next month."
